DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The rreeaallppaatthh() function resolves all symbolic links, extra “/” characters
     and references to _/_._/ and _/_._._/ in _p_a_t_h_n_a_m_e, and copies the resulting ab‐
     solute pathname into the memory pointed to by _r_e_s_o_l_v_e_d___p_a_t_h.  The
     _r_e_s_o_l_v_e_d___p_a_t_h argument _m_u_s_t point to a buffer capable of storing at least
     PATH_MAX characters, or be NULL.

     The rreeaallppaatthh() function will resolve both absolute and relative paths and
     return the absolute pathname corresponding to _p_a_t_h_n_a_m_e.  All components
     of _p_a_t_h_n_a_m_e must exist when rreeaallppaatthh() is called, and all but the last
     component must name either directories or symlinks pointing to the direc‐
